# Android upload-keystore configuration — TEMPLATE (safe to commit).
#
# Copy this file to `key.properties` (same directory, `app/android/`) and fill
# in the real values to build a SIGNED release APK locally:
#
#     cp key.properties.example key.properties
#
# The real `key.properties` — and any `*.jks` / `*.keystore` file — is GITIGNORED
# (see app/android/.gitignore); never commit your keystore or its passwords.
# When `key.properties` is absent, `app/android/app/build.gradle.kts` refuses to
# assemble a release build — it fails with a clear error — rather than silently
# signing the "release" with the debug key. Debug builds and `flutter test` do
# not need a keystore.
#
# In CI the forthcoming release job (see docs/dev/releasing.md, "Android (signed
# APK)") reconstructs this file from repository secrets — the keystore is decoded
# from ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 and the fields below map to the matching secrets.
#
# Fields (all four are required when signing a release):
#
#   storePassword  Password for the keystore file          (CI: ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD)
#   keyPassword    Password for the key entry / alias       (CI: ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD)
#   keyAlias       Alias of the key inside the keystore     (CI: ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS)
#   storeFile      Path to the keystore file (.jks)         (decoded from ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64)
#                  A relative path is resolved from app/android/.

storePassword=your-keystore-password
keyPassword=your-key-password
keyAlias=upload
storeFile=callerscompendium-upload.jks
